# ged, the mouse-oriented text editor of ipl_gpacks (ged.icn with its modules control.icn and textedit.icn), run as the package runs it, on its
# own staged source:
# argument 1 ged.icn
# The script types text at a clicked place, selects a word with a double click and cuts it, pastes it elsewhere, selects with a mouse drag and
# deletes, undoes twice and redoes once, finds a string and replaces another through the prompt window, writes a copy of the buffer to t.txt,
# and quits without saving the edited source. Its commands are control keys. A prompt window opens once under the pointer and stays at that
# place, so the pointer is left where it stood at the first prompt and every later prompt has it inside.
# the insertion point at the end of the Name line, then typed text
click 1 140 32
wait
type  edited
wait
# a double click selects the word Title; control x cuts it
click 1 62 58
click 1 62 58
wait
keydown Control_L
key x
keyup Control_L
wait
# a click at the end of the Date line, control v pastes
click 1 200 110
wait
keydown Control_L
key v
keyup Control_L
wait
# a mouse drag selects part of the date; Delete removes it
drag 1 100 110 180 110
wait
key Delete
wait
# control z twice: the deletion and then the paste are undone; control y redoes the paste
keydown Control_L
key z
keyup Control_L
wait
keydown Control_L
key z
keyup Control_L
wait
keydown Control_L
key y
keyup Control_L
wait
# control f: the prompt window asks the string; the match is selected
keydown Control_L
key f
keyup Control_L
wait
type Links
key Return
wait
# control r: replace, asked in two lines of the prompt window
keydown Control_L
key r
keyup Control_L
wait
type textedit
key Return
wait
type widget
key Return
wait
# control d: write a copy of the buffer to a typed file name
keydown Control_L
key d
keyup Control_L
wait
type t.txt
key Return
wait
# control q: quit; the buffer is changed, so it asks, and d answers don't save
keydown Control_L
key q
keyup Control_L
wait
key d
